        ],
        "motion_energy": 27.72,
        "script": "Calling is this sense of what I'm meant to do. I believe that if you're religious, this is something you need to give up. Something I've said from the very beginning is, Lord, guide my path. Make your will my will. I've also, to find my calling, I've walked the community of Santiago, which is ancient practice, not just for Catholics, but for all religions. When you don't know what to do, go for a super long walk. We are an ambulatory species. We're made to walk and we find things and we think better when we walk. There's a ton of research on this. And so I've walked across Northern Spain twice in 2019 and with my wife. Did it again in 2021 when I have these big intentions and these big questions. But the whole point is that you need openness so that the answers can actually find you. Then what I talk about with young people is do something. Just do something."
      },
